    "narrative": "The Austin Waves' offensive engine today centers on high-upside matchups against mediocre arms, led by **Kyle Tucker** (74.54) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (72.37). **Kyle Tucker** remains our most reliable asset against Eduardo Rodriguez; despite the lineup being pending, the combination of a favorable SP_xERA of 4.53 and the high-leverage #5 spot provides a strong scoring floor. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** presents a fascinating case\u2014despite a slight BvP penalty from his 25-PA sample against Sandy Alcantara, his massive dynamic platoon advantage (+14%) and the high-value #2 spot in the order elevate him to our second-best play. We are also monitoring **Nasim Nunez** (59.34), who, despite the typical #9 hitter penalty, captures significant value due to his elite sprint speed and a high-probability SB opportunity against Alcantara\u2019s slower delivery, which aligns perfectly with our organizational emphasis on speed.\n\nThe depth of the roster means difficult choices, with **Josh Jung** (56.59) narrowly securing the 3B start over potential utility options. While **Liam Hicks** (52.97) and **Sam Antonacci** (45.07) are forced into action against a tough Joe Ryan, their placement at the top of the lineup helps mitigate the risk of Ryan\u2019s 3.21 xERA. **Andy Pages** (70.53) rounds out our strongest tier, benefiting from a favorable platoon setup against the lefty Rodriguez. With **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Jackson Merrill** all off today, our bench remains stagnant. **Luis Robert Jr.** remains firmly sidelined on the IL, leaving our secondary depth\u2014**Jordan Westburg**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Drake Baldwin**, **Jorge Polanco**, **Josh Lowe**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Nolan Schanuel**, **Miguel Andujar**, **Coby Mayo**, **Brayan Rocchio**, and **Dominic Smith**\u2014ready to rotate as we manage our total games played and look to maximize efficiency across the rest of the week.",
